    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0106" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/1869½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State ad interim</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">17 June, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Of course we understand
                    that the British Government cannot defend our people or our Embassy against
                    these air raids; but we also understand, as Sir Cecil does not when he is under
                    great excitement, that it is none of our business to protest against these
                    methods of “warfare”, no matter what our opinion of them may be.</p>
                <pb facs="0107" n="39" xml:id="pg39"/>
                <p>I feel a great deal of sympathy with the Ambassador, and am quite willing to let
                    these incidents pass with a complete understanding of how they occur.</p>
                <p>Cordially yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
